# Read-only moving aim findings, candidate scope only

| Concrete blocker / source location | Minimum deliberate change |
| --- | --- |
| T2 `native_adapter.py:159`, `adapters.py:163`, `deployment/profile.py:235` permit red_sentry only; native packet215 fixes red/team7. | For this next experiment keep **red_sentry** only and old stationary ID/profile. A separate trusted-local opt-in registration may declare a new moving candidate. Other roles/team support is a later change; CPP main188–192 supports team-based detector colors already. |
| T2 native_adapter167–174 checks speed/yaw≤.03, anchor≤.025m and stable.4s; invalid motion closes its model process. Runtime682–688 also removes gimbal for requested/measured motion when stationary_only. | New candidate needs coordinated adapter policy plus descriptor/runtime acceptance. Movement itself must return a bounded inactive/pending response when outside reviewed scope, not unload/reload the model each WASD/nav tick. Keep original permissions, episode/epoch, freshness80, SDK150, limit checks and no auto fire. |
| Capture transform exists: rmcs_contract13–19 builds baseyaw+gimbalyaw/pitch quaternion and joint-rate gyro; native_adapter214–215 uses original captured own state. Command converter32–35 uses current baseyaw to produce servo yaw. | Preserve this path. Verify against actual compiled MuJoCo body matrix/Jacobian, and test capture/current baseyaw changes without retiming. Do not replace direction with target-truth atan2. |
| Frozen CPP main156–160 consumes quaternion/local gyro;187 applies rotated camera lever arm. It does **not** read serialized base odom linear velocity/yaw_origin translation. | Rotation compensation is present; arbitrary translating/accelerating-shooter correctness is unproved. Constant-velocity relative-target tracking can be meaningful because simulated bullets inherit muzzle Jacobian velocity (match_engine133). Do not call omitted explicit translation automatically a proven bug or claim full moving support. Use a narrowly declared candidate and actual physical fixtures. |
| PB source03 capture_feedback80–82 rejects v>.06 or yaw-rate>.25 and publish155–158 returns pending without image. Registration aim_plugin106–111 does not actually set stationary_only descriptor. | Internal PB limit must be reflected honestly in UI capabilities; missing descriptor is not support for moving. Keep Source03 sealed. A future Source04 needs explicit captured-own ego frame semantics rather than only removing its speed check. |
| PB tracker frame is chassis-fixed gimbal_aim_origin (pb_aim_stack55); dynamic TF169–171 uses only gimbal q3/q4. Original tracker199–240 transforms into this frame and estimates velocities. pb_aim_contract28–35 assumes returned yaw is already chassis-relative. | Turning chassis moves those axes and can contaminate target motion. Source04 should use an explicitly defined local inertial/odometry frame derived **only from allowed captured own sensors**, static calibration and original capture stamps; convert algorithm output explicitly back to current base orientation. No ideal enemy/map poses, latest TF attachment or new deadline. |
| PB solver uses original speed18 (PB_AIM_PARAMS62); sim infantry bullet22.5, hero12 (match_engine124). | Do not claim ballistic calibration for a different weapon. If later adjusting own-weapon calibration, require fresh declared deployment/source provenance; do not edit sealed source03 YAML or infer enemy truth. Manual firing stays manual. |

First controlled moving checks should use actual actuator-driven red_sentry motion with the unchanged scene and model: constant .25m/s lateral translation, then .2rad/s yaw, then start/stop. Original500Hz,15fps,1440x1080,80/150 remain. Every exposure is fresh; tracker receives genuine consecutive frames, never dummy warm inputs. A static opposing robot is only scene setup; enemy truth is evaluator-only. Assess actual direction/consumption and manually authorized shots separately. A unit-level transform oracle can compare captured quaternion and gyro against compiled body xmat and rotational Jacobian, using own joints only.

No source patch, model run or moving qualification is performed in this review. Root now owns the playable manual Infantry + navigation/decision Sentry + tree-opponents3v3 implementation; repairing every family's JSON serialization is not a prerequisite to delivering that manual game.
